Yes, you can send multiple care contexts in a single request. The `careContexts` field in the request body is an array, so you can include multiple visits. The `count` field should match the number of care contexts you're sending.

Here's the structure:

```json
{
  "abhaAddress": "<ABHA_ADDRESS>",
  "patient": [
    {
      "referenceNumber": "TMH-PUID-001",
      "display": "Patient Name",
      "count": 2,
      "hiTypes": "OPConsultation",
      "careContexts": [
        {
          "referenceNumber": "visit-001",
          "display": "Visit 1"
        },
        {
          "referenceNumber": "visit-002",
          "display": "Visit 2"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

See the [POST /api/hiecm/hip/v3/link/carecontext](https://developer.abdm.gov.in/docs/hiecm/v3/api/m2/endpoints/m2-post-hip-v3-link-carecontext) endpoint on the developer portal for the full specification.

